# Cloudflare routing.
# Format: <from> <to> <status>. First match wins.
#
# There are NO 200 rewrites here, on purpose. Cloudflare Pages does not
# honour a rewrite whose target is an .html file: it applies its own clean
# URL redirect to the extensionless form instead. A rule like
#
#     /es    /indexES.html    200
#
# came back as "307 -> /indexES", and the 301 that sent /indexES on to /es
# closed the circle. Every Spanish page sat in a redirect loop.
#
# So the filename IS the slug now: es.html, contacto.html, preguntas.html,
# ayuda.html, aviso-legal.html, descargar.html. Pages serves each at its
# clean path with a plain 200, exactly as it already did for the English
# pages, and this file is left with nothing but the legacy redirects.

# The old Spanish URLs, kept working so anything indexed or bookmarked
# lands on the right page instead of a 404.
/indexES.html      /es             301
/contactES.html    /contacto       301
/faqES.html        /preguntas      301
/helpES.html       /ayuda          301
/legalES.html      /aviso-legal    301
/downloadES.html   /descargar      301

# Same again for the extensionless form those filenames used to produce.
/indexES        /es                301
/contactES      /contacto          301
/faqES          /preguntas         301
/helpES         /ayuda             301
/legalES        /aviso-legal       301
/downloadES     /descargar         301

# The old home page file.
/index.html     /                  301
